-- title:
--   Frobenius series has kernel of degree r^{2k}
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime, let $B$ be a commutative Noetherian ring, and let $k$ be a natural number. Consider the pair of power series $\varphi =$ `Rigidified.frobSeries` $B\,k$ in two variables over $B$, namely the element of $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to B[[X_0,X_1]]$ whose $i$-th component is $X_i^{r^k}$. The theorem asserts that $\varphi$ has kernel of degree $r^{2k}$ in the sense of `FormalODModule.HasKernelOfDegree`, i.e. that the three following statements hold for the kernel algebra $B[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0^{r^k},X_1^{r^k})$, the quotient of $B[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by the range of $\varphi$: it is a finite $B$-module; it is a projective $B$-module; and for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f : B \to \kappa$, the $\kappa$-vector space $\kappa[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0^{r^k},X_1^{r^k})$, obtained as the kernel algebra of the componentwise image of $\varphi$ under the coefficient map induced by $f$, has dimension exactly $r^{2k}$.
--
--   This records the kernel degree of the $k$-th iterate of relative Frobenius on a two-dimensional formal group, the entry of the height bookkeeping used when comparing transports of a rigidification across Frobenius twists in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting. It is cited by the computation of kernel degrees of the $\varpi$- and $\mathcal{O}$-actions and by the rigidification-transport lemmas for fake elliptic curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_hasKernelOfDegree_frobSeries.lean

